*> Automatic differentiation: forward mode (Dual), reverse mode (Tape/Var) and
*> second-order forward mode (HyperDual), ending in Rosenbrock gradient descent.
*> CMD: just TARGET=autodiff_ex run-cobol
*>
*> The C++ example also uses the template drivers datamunge::autodiff::derivative,
*> gradient_forward, gradient_reverse, jacobian_forward and hessian; templates are
*> not bound, so, like the Lua port, this uses the named-method API only.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. AUTODIFF-EX.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
COPY "datamunge.cpy".

*> Operand registers for the arithmetic paragraphs: R = A op B, or R = A * SCALAR.
01 A         USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 B         USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 R         USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 SCALAR    USAGE COMP-2.
*> Inputs for NEW-DUAL, NEW-HYPER-DUAL and NEW-VAR.
01 VAL       USAGE COMP-2.
01 EPS-1     USAGE COMP-2.
01 EPS-2     USAGE COMP-2.
01 TAPE      USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

*> Every handle the arithmetic paragraphs create; FREE-TEMPS closes them all.
01 TEMP-COUNT USAGE BINARY-LONG VALUE 0.
01 TEMP-HANDLE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED OCCURS 200.

*> Rosenbrock f(x0, x1) = (1 - x0)^2 + 100 (x1 - x0^2)^2: inputs RX0, RX1, output FX.
01 RX0       USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 RX1       USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 FX        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 TERM-A    USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.

01 X0        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 VX        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 VY        USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 GRAD      USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED.
01 GX        USAGE COMP-2.
01 GY        USAGE COMP-2.
01 PX        USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.0.
01 PY        USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.0.
01 FA        USAGE COMP-2.
01 FB        USAGE COMP-2.

*> Jacobian of [x^2, xy, y^3] at (2, 3); column seeds (seed_x, seed_y).
01 OUTPUTS.
   05 OUTPUT-HANDLE USAGE BINARY-DOUBLE UNSIGNED OCCURS 3.
01 JACOBIAN.
   05 JAC-I-ROW OCCURS 3.
      10 JAC USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 2.
01 SEED-DATA.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 1.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.0.
   05 FILLER USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 1.0.
01 SEEDS REDEFINES SEED-DATA.
   05 SEED-I-ROW OCCURS 2.
      10 SEED USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 2.
01 HESSIAN.
   05 HESS-I-ROW OCCURS 2.
      10 HESS USAGE COMP-2 OCCURS 2.
01 I-ROW     USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 J-COL     USAGE BINARY-LONG.

*> Gradient descent.
01 POINT-X   USAGE COMP-2.
01 POINT-Y   USAGE COMP-2.
01 LOSS      USAGE COMP-2.
01 LEARNING-RATE USAGE COMP-2 VALUE 0.001.
01 N-STEPS   USAGE BINARY-LONG VALUE 2000.
01 ITER      USAGE BINARY-LONG.

*> Output: build a line in OUT-LINE at OUT-PTR; APPEND-NUM adds NUM to it.
01 OUT-LINE  PIC X(200).
01 OUT-PTR   USAGE BINARY-LONG.
01 INT-1     PIC -(9)9.
01 NUM       USAGE COMP-2.
01 NUM-EDIT  PIC -(12)9.9(10).
01 NUM-TEXT  PIC X(32).
01 NUM-LEN   USAGE BINARY-LONG.

PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    DISPLAY "=================== Forward mode: scalar derivative ==================="
    *> Seed derivative = 1 to read df/dx directly.
    MOVE 2.0 TO VAL
    MOVE 1.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO X0
    *> f(x) = x^3 - 2x
    MOVE X0 TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE X0 TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO TERM-A
    MOVE X0 TO A
    MOVE 2.0 TO SCALAR
    PERFORM DUAL-SCALE
    MOVE TERM-A TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-SUB
    MOVE R TO DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-SELF
    CALL "dm_dual_derivative" USING DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-RESULT TO NUM
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    DISPLAY "f(x) = x^3 - 2x, f'(2) = " NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN) " (exact: 10)"
    PERFORM FREE-TEMPS

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Reverse mode: build a graph by hand ==================="
    CALL "dm_tape_new" USING DM-TAPE-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-TAPE-NEW-RESULT TO TAPE R
    PERFORM KEEP
    MOVE 2.0 TO VAL
    PERFORM NEW-VAR
    MOVE R TO VX
    MOVE 3.0 TO VAL
    PERFORM NEW-VAR
    MOVE R TO VY
    *> y = a*b + sin(a)
    MOVE VX TO A
    MOVE VY TO B
    PERFORM VAR-MUL
    MOVE R TO TERM-A
    MOVE VX TO DM-VAR-SIN-SELF
    CALL "dm_var_sin" USING DM-VAR-SIN DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-SIN-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP
    MOVE TERM-A TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM VAR-ADD
    MOVE R TO FX
    MOVE FX TO DM-VAR-VALUE-SELF
    CALL "dm_var_value" USING DM-VAR-VALUE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-VALUE-RESULT TO NUM
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    DISPLAY "y = a*b + sin(a) at a=2, b=3 -> y = " NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN)
    PERFORM BACKWARD
    MOVE VX TO A
    PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    DISPLAY "dy/da = " NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN) " (exact: b + cos(a))"
    MOVE VY TO A
    PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    DISPLAY "dy/db = " NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN) " (exact: a)"
    PERFORM FREE-TEMPS

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Forward vs reverse mode agree on the Rosenbrock function ==================="
    *> Forward mode: one Dual pass per partial derivative, seeding the direction of interest.
    MOVE PX TO VAL
    MOVE 1.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO RX0
    MOVE PY TO VAL
    MOVE 0.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO RX1
    PERFORM ROSENBROCK-DUAL
    MOVE FX TO DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-SELF
    CALL "dm_dual_derivative" USING DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-RESULT TO GX
    MOVE PX TO VAL
    MOVE 0.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO RX0
    MOVE PY TO VAL
    MOVE 1.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO RX1
    PERFORM ROSENBROCK-DUAL
    MOVE FX TO DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-SELF
    CALL "dm_dual_derivative" USING DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-RESULT TO GY
    PERFORM FREE-TEMPS

    *> Reverse mode: one Tape/Var pass computes every partial at once.
    CALL "dm_tape_new" USING DM-TAPE-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-TAPE-NEW-RESULT TO TAPE R
    PERFORM KEEP
    MOVE PX TO VAL
    PERFORM NEW-VAR
    MOVE R TO RX0
    MOVE PY TO VAL
    PERFORM NEW-VAR
    MOVE R TO RX1
    PERFORM ROSENBROCK-VAR
    PERFORM BACKWARD

    *> The plain-number Rosenbrock value.
    COMPUTE FA = 1.0 - PX
    COMPUTE FB = PY - PX * PX
    COMPUTE NUM = FA * FA + 100.0 * FB * FB
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    DISPLAY "f(0,0) = " NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN)
    PERFORM START-LINE
    STRING "gradient (forward mode): [" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE GX TO NUM
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    STRING ", " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE GY TO NUM
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    PERFORM END-LINE
    PERFORM START-LINE
    STRING "gradient (reverse mode): [" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE RX0 TO A
    PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    STRING ", " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE RX1 TO A
    PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    PERFORM END-LINE
    PERFORM FREE-TEMPS

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Jacobian of a vector-valued function ==================="
    *> f(x,y) = [x^2, xy, y^3] at (2,3) -- one Dual pass per (output, input) pair.
    PERFORM VARYING J-COL FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL J-COL > 2
        MOVE 2.0 TO VAL
        MOVE SEED(J-COL, 1) TO EPS-1
        PERFORM NEW-DUAL
        MOVE R TO RX0
        MOVE 3.0 TO VAL
        MOVE SEED(J-COL, 2) TO EPS-1
        PERFORM NEW-DUAL
        MOVE R TO RX1
        PERFORM VECTOR-FN
        PERFORM VARYING I-ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I-ROW > 3
            MOVE OUTPUT-HANDLE(I-ROW) TO DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-SELF
            CALL "dm_dual_derivative" USING DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE DM-STATUS
            PERFORM CHECK
            MOVE DM-DUAL-DERIVATIVE-RESULT TO JAC(I-ROW, J-COL)
        END-PERFORM
        PERFORM FREE-TEMPS
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY "f(x,y) = [x^2, xy, y^3] at (2,3), Jacobian:"
    PERFORM VARYING I-ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I-ROW > 3
        MOVE JAC(I-ROW, 1) TO FA
        MOVE JAC(I-ROW, 2) TO FB
        PERFORM DISPLAY-PAIR
    END-PERFORM

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Hessian via second-order forward mode (HyperDual) ==================="
    *> One HyperDual pass per (i, j) pair reads off d^2f/dxi dxj directly from eps1eps2,
    *> at the Rosenbrock function's minimum (1, 1).
    PERFORM VARYING I-ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I-ROW > 2
        PERFORM VARYING J-COL FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL J-COL > 2
            MOVE 1.0 TO VAL
            MOVE SEED(I-ROW, 1) TO EPS-1
            MOVE SEED(J-COL, 1) TO EPS-2
            PERFORM NEW-HYPER-DUAL
            MOVE R TO RX0
            MOVE SEED(I-ROW, 2) TO EPS-1
            MOVE SEED(J-COL, 2) TO EPS-2
            PERFORM NEW-HYPER-DUAL
            MOVE R TO RX1
            PERFORM ROSENBROCK-HYPER-DUAL
            MOVE FX TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-EPS1EPS2-SELF
            CALL "dm_hyper_dual_eps1eps2" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-EPS1EPS2 DM-STATUS
            PERFORM CHECK
            MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-EPS1EPS2-RESULT TO HESS(I-ROW, J-COL)
            PERFORM FREE-TEMPS
        END-PERFORM
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY "Hessian of the Rosenbrock function at its minimum (1,1):"
    PERFORM VARYING I-ROW FROM 1 BY 1 UNTIL I-ROW > 2
        MOVE HESS(I-ROW, 1) TO FA
        MOVE HESS(I-ROW, 2) TO FB
        PERFORM DISPLAY-PAIR
    END-PERFORM

    DISPLAY " "
    DISPLAY "=================== Gradient descent driven by reverse-mode gradients ==================="
    *> The classic Rosenbrock starting point.
    MOVE -1.2 TO POINT-X
    MOVE 1.0 TO POINT-Y
    PERFORM VARYING ITER FROM 0 BY 1 UNTIL ITER >= N-STEPS
        CALL "dm_tape_new" USING DM-TAPE-NEW DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-TAPE-NEW-RESULT TO TAPE R
        PERFORM KEEP
        MOVE POINT-X TO VAL
        PERFORM NEW-VAR
        MOVE R TO RX0
        MOVE POINT-Y TO VAL
        PERFORM NEW-VAR
        MOVE R TO RX1
        PERFORM ROSENBROCK-VAR
        PERFORM BACKWARD
        MOVE FX TO DM-VAR-VALUE-SELF
        CALL "dm_var_value" USING DM-VAR-VALUE DM-STATUS
        PERFORM CHECK
        MOVE DM-VAR-VALUE-RESULT TO LOSS
        MOVE RX0 TO A
        PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
        COMPUTE POINT-X = POINT-X - LEARNING-RATE * NUM
        MOVE RX1 TO A
        PERFORM GRADIENT-AT
        COMPUTE POINT-Y = POINT-Y - LEARNING-RATE * NUM
        PERFORM FREE-TEMPS
        IF ITER = 0 OR ITER = N-STEPS - 1
            PERFORM START-LINE
            MOVE ITER TO INT-1
            STRING "step " FUNCTION TRIM(INT-1) ": loss = " DELIMITED BY SIZE
                INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
            MOVE LOSS TO NUM
            PERFORM APPEND-NUM
            STRING ", x = [" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
            MOVE POINT-X TO NUM
            PERFORM APPEND-NUM
            STRING ", " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
            MOVE POINT-Y TO NUM
            PERFORM APPEND-NUM
            PERFORM END-LINE
        END-IF
    END-PERFORM
    DISPLAY "(true minimum is at [1, 1] with loss 0)"
    STOP RUN.

*> FX = Rosenbrock(RX0, RX1) over Duals.
ROSENBROCK-DUAL.
    MOVE 1.0 TO VAL
    MOVE 0.0 TO EPS-1
    PERFORM NEW-DUAL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE RX0 TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO TERM-A
    MOVE RX0 TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE RX1 TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE 100.0 TO SCALAR
    PERFORM DUAL-SCALE
    MOVE TERM-A TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-ADD
    MOVE R TO FX.

*> FX = Rosenbrock(RX0, RX1) over HyperDuals.
ROSENBROCK-HYPER-DUAL.
    MOVE 1.0 TO VAL
    MOVE 0.0 TO EPS-1 EPS-2
    PERFORM NEW-HYPER-DUAL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE RX0 TO B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO TERM-A
    MOVE RX0 TO A B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-MUL
    MOVE RX1 TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE 100.0 TO SCALAR
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-SCALE
    MOVE TERM-A TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM HYPER-DUAL-ADD
    MOVE R TO FX.

*> FX = Rosenbrock(RX0, RX1) over Vars on TAPE.
ROSENBROCK-VAR.
    MOVE 1.0 TO VAL
    PERFORM NEW-VAR
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE RX0 TO B
    PERFORM VAR-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM VAR-MUL
    MOVE R TO TERM-A
    MOVE RX0 TO A B
    PERFORM VAR-MUL
    MOVE RX1 TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM VAR-SUB
    MOVE R TO A B
    PERFORM VAR-MUL
    MOVE R TO A
    MOVE 100.0 TO SCALAR
    PERFORM VAR-SCALE
    MOVE TERM-A TO A
    MOVE R TO B
    PERFORM VAR-ADD
    MOVE R TO FX.

*> OUTPUT-HANDLE(1..3) = [x^2, xy, y^3] for x = RX0, y = RX1 (Duals).
VECTOR-FN.
    MOVE RX0 TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO OUTPUT-HANDLE(1)
    MOVE RX1 TO B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO OUTPUT-HANDLE(2)
    MOVE RX1 TO A B
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO A
    PERFORM DUAL-MUL
    MOVE R TO OUTPUT-HANDLE(3).

*> GRAD = TAPE.backward(FX).
BACKWARD.
    MOVE TAPE TO DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-SELF
    MOVE FX TO DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-OUTPUT
    CALL "dm_tape_backward" USING DM-TAPE-BACKWARD DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-TAPE-BACKWARD-RESULT TO GRAD R
    PERFORM KEEP.

*> NUM = GRAD[A.index()], the gradient of the Var A (index() is 0-based).
GRADIENT-AT.
    MOVE A TO DM-VAR-INDEX-SELF
    CALL "dm_var_index" USING DM-VAR-INDEX DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE GRAD TO DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-SELF
    COMPUTE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-INDEX = DM-VAR-INDEX-RESULT + 1
    CALL "dm_vector_double_get" USING DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VECTOR-DOUBLE-VALUE TO NUM.

*> Dual arithmetic: each result is a new handle, kept for FREE-TEMPS.
NEW-DUAL.
    MOVE 2 TO DM-DUAL-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE VAL TO DM-DUAL-NEW-VALUE
    MOVE EPS-1 TO DM-DUAL-NEW-DERIVATIVE
    CALL "dm_dual_new" USING DM-DUAL-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-NEW-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

DUAL-ADD.
    MOVE A TO DM-DUAL-ADD-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-DUAL-ADD-OTHER
    CALL "dm_dual_add" USING DM-DUAL-ADD DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-ADD-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

DUAL-SUB.
    MOVE A TO DM-DUAL-SUBTRACT-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-DUAL-SUBTRACT-OTHER
    CALL "dm_dual_subtract" USING DM-DUAL-SUBTRACT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-SUBTRACT-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

DUAL-MUL.
    MOVE A TO DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-OTHER
    CALL "dm_dual_multiply" USING DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

DUAL-SCALE.
    MOVE A TO DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SELF
    MOVE SCALAR TO DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SCALAR
    CALL "dm_dual_multiply_scalar" USING DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

*> HyperDual arithmetic.
NEW-HYPER-DUAL.
    MOVE 3 TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-GIVEN
    MOVE VAL TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-VALUE
    MOVE EPS-1 TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-EPS1
    MOVE EPS-2 TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-EPS2
    CALL "dm_hyper_dual_new" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-NEW-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

HYPER-DUAL-ADD.
    MOVE A TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-ADD-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-ADD-OTHER
    CALL "dm_hyper_dual_add" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-ADD DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-ADD-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

HYPER-DUAL-SUB.
    MOVE A TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-SUBTRACT-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-SUBTRACT-OTHER
    CALL "dm_hyper_dual_subtract" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-SUBTRACT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-SUBTRACT-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

HYPER-DUAL-MUL.
    MOVE A TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-OTHER
    CALL "dm_hyper_dual_multiply" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

HYPER-DUAL-SCALE.
    MOVE A TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SELF
    MOVE SCALAR TO DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SCALAR
    CALL "dm_hyper_dual_multiply_scalar" USING DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-HYPER-DUAL-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

*> Var arithmetic, recorded on TAPE.
NEW-VAR.
    MOVE TAPE TO DM-VAR-NEW-TAPE
    MOVE VAL TO DM-VAR-NEW-VALUE
    CALL "dm_var_new" USING DM-VAR-NEW DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-NEW-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

VAR-ADD.
    MOVE A TO DM-VAR-ADD-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-VAR-ADD-OTHER
    CALL "dm_var_add" USING DM-VAR-ADD DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-ADD-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

VAR-SUB.
    MOVE A TO DM-VAR-SUBTRACT-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-VAR-SUBTRACT-OTHER
    CALL "dm_var_subtract" USING DM-VAR-SUBTRACT DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-SUBTRACT-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

VAR-MUL.
    MOVE A TO DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-SELF
    MOVE B TO DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-OTHER
    CALL "dm_var_multiply" USING DM-VAR-MULTIPLY DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

VAR-SCALE.
    MOVE A TO DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SELF
    MOVE SCALAR TO DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-SCALAR
    CALL "dm_var_multiply_scalar" USING DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-SCALAR DM-STATUS
    PERFORM CHECK
    MOVE DM-VAR-MULTIPLY-SCALAR-RESULT TO R
    PERFORM KEEP.

*> Remembers R for FREE-TEMPS.
KEEP.
    ADD 1 TO TEMP-COUNT
    MOVE R TO TEMP-HANDLE(TEMP-COUNT).

*> Closes every kept handle, newest first (Vars before their Tape).
FREE-TEMPS.
    PERFORM UNTIL TEMP-COUNT = 0
        MOVE TEMP-HANDLE(TEMP-COUNT) TO DM-HANDLE-SELF
        CALL "dm_close" USING DM-HANDLE DM-STATUS
        SUBTRACT 1 FROM TEMP-COUNT
    END-PERFORM.

*> Displays "  [FA, FB]".
DISPLAY-PAIR.
    PERFORM START-LINE
    STRING "  [" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE FA TO NUM
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    STRING ", " DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    MOVE FB TO NUM
    PERFORM APPEND-NUM
    PERFORM END-LINE.

START-LINE.
    MOVE SPACES TO OUT-LINE
    MOVE 1 TO OUT-PTR.

*> Ends the line with "]" and displays it.
END-LINE.
    STRING "]" DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR
    DISPLAY OUT-LINE(1:OUT-PTR - 1).

APPEND-NUM.
    PERFORM FORMAT-NUMBER
    STRING NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN) DELIMITED BY SIZE INTO OUT-LINE WITH POINTER OUT-PTR.

*> Formats NUM without trailing zeros into NUM-TEXT(1:NUM-LEN).
FORMAT-NUMBER.
    COMPUTE NUM-EDIT ROUNDED = NUM
    MOVE FUNCTION TRIM(NUM-EDIT) TO NUM-TEXT
    COMPUTE NUM-LEN = FUNCTION LENGTH(FUNCTION TRIM(NUM-TEXT))
    PERFORM UNTIL NUM-TEXT(NUM-LEN:1) NOT = "0"
        SUBTRACT 1 FROM NUM-LEN
    END-PERFORM
    IF NUM-TEXT(NUM-LEN:1) = "."
        SUBTRACT 1 FROM NUM-LEN
    END-IF.

*> Stops with the error after a failed call.
CHECK.
    IF NOT DM-STATUS-OK
        DISPLAY "datamunge error (" FUNCTION TRIM(DM-STATUS-KIND) "): "
            DM-STATUS-MESSAGE(1:DM-STATUS-LENGTH) UPON SYSERR
        STOP RUN RETURNING 1
    END-IF.
